# Pillar 1 — Real Data Ingestion & Validation

Accepts any NSRDB-format CSV
Auto-detects and skips metadata rows
Validates that required columns (GHI, Month, Day, Hour) exist
Reports data quality: missing values, outliers, sensor errors (negative GHI at daytime)


# Pillar 2 — Feature Engineering

Calculates Peak Sun Hours per day from raw hourly GHI
Builds a Monthly Seasonal Profile (12 PSH averages)
Identifies the best and worst solar months of the year
Computes Capacity Factor (actual generation ÷ theoretical maximum)


# Pillar 3 — Solar Generation Modeling

Takes user inputs: panel wattage, count, performance factor
Uses the real monthly PSH (from Pillar 2) instead of a hardcoded guess
Produces a month-by-month energy generation forecast as a DataFrame
Projects 25-year lifetime energy accounting for 0.5% annual panel degradation


# Pillar 4 — Financial Analysis

Gross cost, net investment (after subsidies)
25-year savings trajectory with electricity price escalation
Levelized Cost of Energy (LCOE)
Net Present Value (NPV) and exact payback year
Returns the full financial model as an exportable DataFrame


# Pillar 5 — Visual Report

Plot 1: Monthly GHI bar chart (Seasonal Solar Profile)
Plot 2: 25-year cumulative savings line chart with payback crossover marked
Plot 3: Hourly GHI heatmap (Month × Hour of day) — the one that will genuinely impress people
Saves all charts as PNG files automatically


