What all to report in the Data Quality report-
1. Missing values -
    - Number of missing values per column.
    - and the percentage of missing value in that column
    - Output will be a dictionary.

2. The Duplicates - 
    Duplicate rows can skew analysis and waste the memory.
    - Total count of exact duplicates and the specific subsets of data.

3. Data Types (Data Integrity)-
    E.g. the data points stored as text will break the visualization part
    - The data type of each column e.g., float, integer, object/string, datetime

4. Statistical Summaries and Outliers - 
    - Count, mean, standard deviation, minimums, maximums, and quantiles (25%, 50%, 75%).

5. Zeroes and Negative Values
    - Count of zeroes or unexpected negative values in columns that strictly require positive numbers.